id: pm-review-criterion-coverage-map
title: Map substantive review evidence to declared criteria
description: Add an attributable review coverage map over declared acceptance and risk criteria. Builds on closeout verification; reviewer completion and assurance evaluation remain separate.
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T22:15:24.573Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-23T08:57:51.454Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-23T08:57:51.446Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-22T18:55:20.000Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Quota/skipped notices cover zero criteria; Changed criteria invalidate mappings; Judgments remain explicit and attributable; Typed SDK and compact CLI work without git with typed refusals and remedies; Public tracker copy validation and npm plus Bun CI release gates pass
resolution: "Delivered by https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/pull/27 (merge 51bce9146d77, head 06e893d486fe)"
expected_result: Quota/skipped notices cover zero criteria; Changed criteria invalidate mappings; Judgments remain explicit and attributable; Typed SDK and compact CLI work without git with typed refusals and remedies; Public tracker copy validation and npm plus Bun CI release gates pass
actual_result: "Merged at 2026-10-22T18:55:20Z; no readable required checks, so every completed head check run had to succeed, be neutral or be skipped; successful checks: CodeQL, CodeRabbit, codeql, test (22), test (26)"
comments[20]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T22:15:33.479Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against CLI 2026.10.21 assurance measurement/assertion/gate declarations, pm-ops quality measurement providers, sibling README surfaces, and pm-review round/closeout implementations. Round answers who finished at the exact head; closeout evaluates fresh tests; core assurance owns criterion contracts. No existing review-to-criterion map found. Implement explicit acceptance-criterion bindings, including risk criteria declared there, with revision and source digests, exact evidence excerpts, recorded judgment/reason and PM comment attribution. Read maps offline without git, provider calls or writes. Base is PR #25; merge after it. Targeted local gates only due host load; full npm and Bun release gates in CI."
  "2026-10-21T22:23:43.379Z",codex-agent,"Implementation and targeted validation complete. SDK reviewCoverage/coverCriterion and CLI review coverage/cover preserve explicit PM attribution, contract and source digests, exact excerpts and typed remedies. Latest pinned pm linked-test run passes 9/9, zero failures/skips; test-result persistence remains disabled by project policy. Three independent behavioral-revert probes retain the tests and force notice eligibility, remove only the contract revision guard, or blank judgment author/date: each exits 1 with an AssertionError. Exact selectors and aggregate dogfood results are in docs/criterion-coverage-validation.md. Public origin/main tracker at 68eea9cccf2a32c0f101cb85ce8b2f58369f600e: 45 items, 22 findings, 15 criterion-bearing items, 79 criteria, zero mappings, zero reviewed and 79 unreviewed; 30 typed missing-contract refusals. Largest JSON 1753 bytes; total 9678 bytes. Non-git copy with empty PATH and ceiling: measured tracker fingerprints unchanged after SDK cache priming. Early probe observed only SDK runtime-cache/usage additions; no source item or history changed. Initial targeted failures exposed an empty-body eligibility edge and fixture expectations about SDK attribution normalization; corrected runs pass. Full npm/Bun gates reserved for CI."
  "2026-10-21T22:26:14.391Z",codex-agent,"Final self-review found and corrected an explicit retraction edge: global comment deduplication suppressed a reviewed assessment after a gap when it reused the same earlier wording. Every cover request now appends its explicit assessment; the regression replays identical options before and after a gap. An isolated source copy restoring only ifAbsent deduplication fails the retained attribution/retraction test with exit 1 and AssertionError. No change to criterion or evidence validation. PR #27 is ready for review; full CI is running."
  "2026-10-21T22:30:24.955Z",codex-agent,"Packed CI acceptance exposed pinned-host integration boundaries after npm source gates passed 174/174 with all 28 sources at 100/100/100/100: generated --review-pr and --review-url fields are classified as flag typos before extension handling. The fixture now uses canonical --field name=value. Local installed acceptance then exposed injected SDK default author pm-extension overriding the caller environment. Coverage now forwards explicit global author or PM_AUTHOR to the comment mutation; SDK options support an explicit author override. Added direct override and fallback dispatch assertions. An isolated revert removing only author forwarding fails the retained gap-source test with exit 1 and AssertionError. Final targeted source run passes 9/9 with both new modules at 100/100/100/100. Failed CI runs remain failed evidence, not release approval. No upstream issues filed."
  "2026-10-21T22:31:31.062Z",codex-agent,"Installed acceptance now confirms cover reads/writes, explicit caller attribution and typed refusal exits. A subsequent baseline status fixture correctly detected the new synthetic finding as pending because both fixtures used PR 1. Isolated the coverage evidence on synthetic PR 2, leaving baseline round/status PR 1 and its assertions unchanged. This is fixture scope isolation, not a weakened production gate. Rerunning the packed npm/Bun acceptance and final CI; no full local release gate."
  "2026-10-21T22:35:17.568Z",codex-agent,"Reviewer reproduction confirmed a false refusal for substantive severity-marked quota and rate-limit counter findings. Narrowed the coverage guard from topic words to exhausted/reached/skipped/unavailable service-notice phrases. New real-tracker test accepts allowance/quota/rate-limit findings through both SDK and registered review cover, while rejecting four genuine notice variants with typed nonzero remedies. A sixth isolated behavioral revert restores only the old topic denylist and fails with exit 1 and AssertionError. Existing issue #14 owns the broader round-classifier topic; no duplicate issue is created."
  "2026-10-21T22:41:36.375Z",codex-agent,"Source head e8f102d7a1e459e7d89d11a253b3c6fc77cceae4 is green in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-review/actions/runs/39687725734 . npm release-gate steps on Node 22/26 and full bun run release:check each pass 175/175 outer source tests, zero failures/skips, all 28 authored sources at 100/100/100/100. Packed npm/npx plus native Bun/bunx acceptance passes 1/1 in each npm job and again in the Bun gate. Duplication 0% (0/6461 lines, 43 sources, zero clones); 90/90 declarations across 28 files documented. Fresh CI tracker health/history, identity/privacy, typecheck, lint, audit, packaging, changelog and attestation checks pass. Local targeted source suite passes 10/10; npm run test:install passes 1/1 across both consumers; no full local release gate ran. Six isolated behavioral controls fail with AssertionError when restored. Read-only public dogfood: 45 items, 22 findings, 79 criteria, zero explicit coverage, 79 unreviewed, unchanged measured tracker bytes. PR #27 remains ready for review, depends on #25 and must merge after it. Releasing the claim; keep the feature in progress for orchestrator verification. No merge or release. Final documentation/PM receipt commit CI will be verified and linked in the PR. Host UX boundaries encountered are documented; no upstream issue filed."
  "2026-10-22T12:15:59.573Z",codex-agent,"PR #27 review round: pulled remote 48a1bad, then merged current main 260d41c after squash merge of #25. GitHub returns zero review threads and zero reviews, so there are no Outside diff range findings. Resolved README, exports, dispatcher and acceptance conflicts by retaining only coverage additions over current main; CHANGELOG.md is regenerated from tracker data. Content checks passed: 10 coverage feature files retain the original PR contents; 12 shared closeout/test/toolchain files exactly match main. Full-diff self-review checked criterion/source invalidation, notice eligibility, explicit attribution, gaps/retractions and no-git behavior without establishing an additional defect. Plan: run retained source regressions, behavioral dispatch-omission proof, npm plus Bun full release checks at unchanged thresholds, isolated Git identity reproduction, tracker health and final generated changelog. No dist files are tracked."
  "2026-10-22T12:18:34.709Z",codex-agent,"Merge-resolution regression evidence: node --test test/coverage.test.ts passed 10/10, zero failures/skips, including non-git SDK/CLI behavior. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"extension activation exposes all commands\" test/core.test.ts passed 1/1. In a disposable source copy, reverting only registerReviewCommands to current main fails that same retained activation test with AssertionError 9 !== 11, exit 1; the original worktree was unchanged. An initial probe selected the separate schema test and passed, so it is not counted as a revert proof; the corrected activation selector is the valid proof. Initial health with extensions disabled passed all 10 checks; no merge receipts were pending. npm ci passed with zero vulnerabilities. Full npm/Bun gates remain pending; existing source tests and thresholds are unchanged."
  "2026-10-22T12:31:37.087Z",codex-agent,"The first isolated npm release gate passed 175/175 source tests, all 28 sources at 100/100/100/100, and every stage before packed acceptance; packed acceptance failed because the outer linked-test host supplied PM_SOURCE_WORKSPACE_ROOT for the package. consumerEnv inherited that root, so installed closeout looked outside the independent consumer and reported proof.md absent plus a failed linked test. This is an acceptance fixture provenance leak, not a host-load timeout. Fix consumerEnv to bind source provenance to its own cwd, and deliberately supply the outer package root in the packed regression so direct and PM-linked runs both exercise isolation. Shared closeout implementation remains identical to main. Retain the failed gate as evidence; retry the full gates after a targeted packed run and function-only revert control."
  "2026-10-22T12:37:07.476Z",codex-agent,"Consumer provenance behavioral revert proof: an independent disposable source copy retained the new outer-root regression and all production code, restoring only consumerEnv to the pre-fix function. node --test --test-reporter=spec test/install.acceptance.ts exited 1 with AssertionError, artifact_missing and proof.md in the installed closeout result. This is the same failure observed in the first full npm gate. The original worktree was unchanged by the probe. The fixed pm-linked npm run test:install run is still pending; do not treat the negative control as a passing baseline. No source implementation or thresholds changed."
  "2026-10-22T12:51:19.111Z",codex-agent,"Final source 9989ba3 release receipt: env HOME=$(mktemp -d) GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 npm run release:check and bun run release:check both passed all 12 stages at unchanged thresholds. Each passed 175/175 outer source tests and 1/1 packed npm/npx plus native Bun/bunx acceptance, zero failures/skips/cancellations. All 28 authored sources: statements and lines 2653/2653, functions 149/149, branches 1371/1371, all 100 percent. Duplication 0/6465 lines across 43 sources, zero clones; 90 declarations documented; production audit zero vulnerabilities; package allowlist 73 files; attestation check passed without publishing. PM-linked npm run test:install also passed 1/1 with the deliberate outer-source-root regression. Both function-only revert controls failed as intended, and restored baselines passed. The initial npm attempt failed packed acceptance due to the now-corrected fixture defect, not a timeout; no host-load timeout occurred. No new pm CLI/SDK bug established or filed. Existing normal-home global extension version mismatch is an environment limitation; isolated health is authoritative for package integrity. Keep feature in_progress for orchestrator verification; release the working claim and regenerate/check the changelog after this receipt."
  "2026-10-22T14:45:41.200Z",codex-agent,"New review round for PR #27: pulled unchanged remote ddce5e9; current main 260d41c is already an ancestor. The worktree was clean and prior feature/revert/gate receipts remain intact. GitHub returned one unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOVGABD86vPQ3P with its complete comment and no Outside diff range findings in the latest review. Verified the finding: eligible uses an unanchored full notice denylist, falsely refusing substantive severity-marked findings that discuss quota exceeded, rate-limit reached, no access or failed to generate. Reuse this feature item; add real non-git SDK and registered-command cases for every notice alternative, complete notice boundaries and quoted, heading, bullet, bold and newline forms. Run the retained test against the old function first, then narrow only this coverage predicate, record the function-only revert proof, self-review the whole PR and run both complete release gates at unchanged thresholds. No dependency bump, thread interaction or shared round-classifier change is needed."
  "2026-10-22T14:48:15.276Z",codex-agent,"Thread PRRT_kwDOVGABD86vPQ3P regression and revert proof: before the fix, node --test --test-name-pattern=\"substantive quota and rate-limit\" test/coverage.test.ts failed with AssertionError on the substantive quota-exceeded error finding. The corrected PM-linked selector passes 1/1, exercising 56 real non-git scenarios through both SDK and registered CLI: 28 substantive findings accepted and 28 complete notices refused. Every existing notice alternative has substantive and notice controls, with additional leading-clause, quoted, heading, bullet, bold, LF and CRLF cases. node --test test/coverage.test.ts passes 10/10, no failures/skips. In a disposable source copy retaining all new tests, restoring only eligible from ddce5e9 fails the same named regression with AssertionError on the quota-exceeded finding, exit 1; the original worktree is unchanged. Full-diff self-review found the same substring defect throughout this one predicate, now anchored uniformly with complete-clause boundaries. Existing shared classifier and round-completion limitations remain owned by issue #14 and are outside this coverage correction; no new duplicate or SDK defect was established. Next: complete npm and Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-22T14:54:21.202Z",codex-agent,"Self-review extended PRRT_kwDOVGABD86vPQ3P to the severity-prefix formats already recognized by the package. The initial anchored correction passed all 56 scenarios and source coverage, but an added italic-severity regression demonstrated a false acceptance of a Review unavailable notice. Stopped that owned verification run before completion to include italic labels, plain severity labels and image priority badges. It is incomplete evidence, not a passing release gate or a host-load timeout. The predicate now preserves these notice refusals using the same complete-clause boundaries. Final regression has 60 real SDK/registered-command scenarios (28 substantive, 32 notices). Rerun both full gates after this refinement; retain original and intermediate failure evidence."
  "2026-10-22T14:55:57.556Z",codex-agent,"Final PRRT_kwDOVGABD86vPQ3P regression receipt: PM-linked classification selector passed 1/1; full node --test test/coverage.test.ts passed 10/10, zero failures/skips. The final 60 scenarios run through both real non-git SDK and registered CLI paths: 28 substantive findings eligible, 32 genuine notices refused, including bold/italic severity, plain severity labels, linked/unlinked priority badges, quotes, headings, bullets and LF/CRLF. Two independent disposable copies retain the final tests and restore only eligible: ddce5e9 fails with AssertionError on the substantive quota-exceeded finding; c67c05c fails with AssertionError on the italic Review unavailable notice. Both exit 1; the original worktree remains unchanged. This supersedes the earlier 56-scenario baseline for final acceptance. Preserve the intentionally interrupted verification attempt as incomplete, then run fresh full npm and Bun release gates on this refinement."
  "2026-10-22T15:08:51.375Z",codex-agent,"Final review-round gate receipt for PRRT_kwDOVGABD86vPQ3P at source 723ba81: env HOME=$(mktemp -d) GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 npm run release:check and bun run release:check both passed all 12 stages at unchanged thresholds. Each passed 175/175 outer source tests and 1/1 packed npm/npx plus native Bun/bunx acceptance, with zero failures/skips/cancellations. Coverage across 28 authored sources: statements/lines 2653/2653, functions 149/149, branches 1372/1372, all 100 percent. Duplication 0/6488 lines across 43 sources and zero clones; 90 declarations documented; production audit zero vulnerabilities; package allowlist and attestation checks passed. PM-linked classification selector passed 1/1 across 60 real SDK/registered-command scenarios (28 substantive accepted, 32 notices refused); full coverage suite passed 10/10. Both final function-only revert controls failed as intended and the restored baseline passed. The earlier attempt intentionally stopped for additional severity-prefix controls is incomplete evidence and is not included in these pass counts. No host-load timeout occurred. No new pm CLI/SDK defect or UX gap established; existing round-classifier issue #14 remains separate. Keep this feature in_progress for orchestrator verification, release the claim, and regenerate/check the changelog after this receipt. No thread replies/resolutions, PR merge or release is part of this work."
  "2026-10-22T16:42:17.285Z",codex-agent,"New review round: pulled clean unchanged remote 5657ced; main 260d41c is already an ancestor. Prior PRRT_kwDOVGABD86vPQ3P is resolved upstream; one new unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOVGABD86vR6GO was fetched with its complete comment. Latest CodeRabbit review contains no Outside diff range findings. Verified the new finding: eligible applies isInformational to all source bodies, so unmarked substantive topic mentions are refused before the explicit notice guard. Reuse this feature item. Add paired marked/unmarked real-import SDK and registered-command cases, preserving explicit summary boilerplate and every provider-notice family previously filtered by the import classifier. Re-import a stable source identity to exercise classification/content invalidation without growing the fixture inventory. Separate coverage summary/notice eligibility from import verdict heuristics; keep shared round-classifier issue #14 outside this change. Record a function-only revert proof and run both complete release gates at unchanged thresholds after self-review."
  "2026-10-22T16:48:50.963Z",codex-agent,"PRRT_kwDOVGABD86vR6GO regression receipt: the old eligible function failed the new unmarked substantive-finding test with AssertionError on an unmarked quota-exceeded finding (false !== true). The corrected final PM-linked node --test test/coverage.test.ts run passes 11/11, zero failures/skips. Classification diagnostics cover 170 real-import scenarios through both SDK and registered CLI: the retained 60 marked scenarios plus 110 unmarked/topic, explicit-summary and provider-notice scenarios. Explicit zero-finding summaries stay refused; marked or positive-count actionable review bodies remain eligible; known provider families with additional detail remain refused. Imported informational verdicts do not veto explicit judgments on substantive text. A disposable copy retaining the new tests restored only eligible from 5657ced and failed the same named regression with AssertionError, exit 1; the original worktree was unchanged. Typecheck, build:test, lint and zero-duplication checks pass. Full-diff self-review found the same broad topic veto in this one coverage predicate; shared import classification, round behavior, closeout implementation and dependency pins remain identical to main. The first fixture syntax error was corrected before behavioral reproduction and is not counted as revert evidence. Next: both full release gates at unchanged thresholds, then final tracker health/changelog and handoff."
  "2026-10-22T16:59:43.072Z",codex-agent,"Final PRRT_kwDOVGABD86vR6GO gate receipt at source b8afa51: env HOME=$(mktemp -d) GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 npm run release:check and bun run release:check both passed all 12 stages at unchanged thresholds. Each passed 176/176 outer source tests and 1/1 packed npm/npx plus native Bun/bunx acceptance; zero failures/skips/cancellations. All 28 authored sources are at 100 percent: statements/lines 2656/2656, functions 149/149, branches 1374/1374. Duplication is 0/6541 lines across 43 sources with zero clones; all 90 declarations documented; production audit zero vulnerabilities; packaging and attestation passed without publishing. Both runs retain measured diagnostics for all 170 real-import SDK/registered-command cases: 74 substantive/actionable accepted and 96 notice/boilerplate refused. The PM-linked coverage suite passed 11/11. The function-only eligible revert proof failed with AssertionError as intended, and the corrected baseline passed. No host-load timeout occurred. No new pm CLI/SDK defect or UX gap established; shared import/round issue #14 remains separate. Keep this feature in_progress for orchestrator verification, release the claim and regenerate/check the changelog after this receipt. No review reply/resolution, PR merge or release is authorized."
